WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.860
Mystery Quest, a message to you from the Great Wizard.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:26.800
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:28.640
I'm Mike. I'm Sean.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:29.800
I'm Joe.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.180
And I'm Sam.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:36.680
You know, the entire back of the box is that message from the Great Wizard.

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:41.200
So I'm just going to pass on all that, but that's why it doesn't really make that much

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:44.840
sense. The Mystery Quest is not the message.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:50.080
The Mystery Quest actually is not a mystery at all, because it is the quest to become a

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:53.400
wizard. So why didn't they just call it Wizard Quest?

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:57.940
I thought that he already had the basic wizarding training.

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:03.540
And this was just like him trying it all out, you know?

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:06.000
I think he's a junior wizard.

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:08.520
Okay. I mean, that's still like a wizard.

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:11.420
It's like a Hogwarts level wizard.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:13.360
Okay. Yeah, I get that.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:17.820
Yeah. Do you think that was premature of Hagrid to tell Harry he's a wizard?

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:19.200
I think. Like, you really didn't know anything.

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:21.180
Yeah. Oh, you're a PhD.

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:23.560
Like, wizard is like a rank. Student?

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:27.980
Yeah. Okay. Are you upset that it's called Mystery Quest, but the quest is not a mystery?

00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:31.040
I'm just upset at the name in general.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:35.400
It's just kind of, it feels very last minute to me.

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:42.440
Especially when you consider that this game is a, like, it had like a Famicom version that

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:47.140
was much more, like, involved and had a bigger title and everything like that.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:49.080
I wish I had that information freehand, but I don't.

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:53.940
But, like, the idea that, like, they took this game that was about, like, a witch boy

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:58.220
who had a broomstick and everything like that and then just was like, no, this is just a

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:03.860
kid who's got somewhat magical powers, but now he's on a quest to become a wizard.

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:08.420
It just feels like, I don't know, were wizards a big thing in 1989?

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:10.800
The wizard movie was coming out, right?

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:15.480
Also, it wasn't, like, I mean, are we in, like, still in somewhat of, like, Dungeons

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:17.260
and Dragons territory and stuff, too?

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:21.540
Oh, yeah, with these early RPG-ish games, yeah.

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:23.520
What is the wizard's movie?

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:27.280
The wizard? Isn't that the movie where they revealed Super Mario Bros.

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:32.020
3? Yeah, that's, like, the video game movie, right?

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:33.100
Okay. Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:34.020
It has nothing to do with it.

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:36.060
Oh! Yeah. I see.

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:40.360
But, you know, it's 1989, everybody's looking forward to that movie to get, like, their first

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:41.440
view at Super Mario Bros.

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:46.320
3. It's crazy that that was, like, that year's E3 was, like, at the movie theaters.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:56.020
E3, 89. So, this is a, you know, how do you want to, it's, because it's not, it's mostly a platformer,

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:58.860
but it does have some RPG-ish elements to it.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:05.540
So, I'm going to say adventure game, where you play as, um, do they give him a name?

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:07.860
Is he just boy? Like, I can't remember.

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:09.480
Or H-A-O.

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:12.560
Okay. I think I heard some words there, Sean.

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:14.140
What's his name? How?

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:17.760
H-A-O. I don't know how to pronounce it, but, yeah.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:18.560
How could I forget?

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:19.540
I think you pronounce it like how.

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:21.400
I thought it was H-A-O.

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:24.620
Jesus. But I could be wrong.

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:27.280
How could I forget a name like that?

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:35.980
Anyway, um, so you're playing as him, and you have, like, you know, the most, the, all

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:40.880
the enemies are, like, real life encounter things, like scorpions and snakes and stuff

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:43.620
like that. Porcupines. But they're also all the same size.

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:47.280
Yeah. Yeah, like, the bats and everything.

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:54.120
So, there's, you know, I'm a little confused off the bat about this game in the sense of,

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:56.500
like, where do we even start talking?

00:03:56.660 --> 00:04:00.800
Like, what's the actual, what sets this, what is different about this game?

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:02.920
What would you say is the standout feature?

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:05.180
This is finally the game that broke mic.

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:09.000
Well, I guess I'm just stumped on, like, you know, if I talk about it enough, people are

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:13.380
going to think it's either, like, you know, it's like this game or it's like that game.

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:17.260
I can't really tell what makes Mystery Quest, like, what's the defining thing?

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:22.000
The defining feature that, like, you would buy this instead of a different adventure game.

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:23.900
May I? Yes, please.

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:29.860
I think that this, this game is, I mean, it's, despite its name, which makes me think it's

00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:32.760
going to be an RPG or something, it's a, it's a platformer, right?

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:40.040
Right. And what to me makes it different is that, is not necessarily a positive thing, but is

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:46.640
that, like, the, the controls are, like, it's like they tried to pay more attention to physics

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:52.200
or something, or like, like, have their own physics, but it, it comes, it ends up being

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:53.660
very, like, not intuitive.

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:57.560
I don't know if that was, like, everybody else's, like, first impression of this game,

00:04:57.640 --> 00:05:01.420
but for me it was, like, a platformer where the platforming was, like, trying to do something

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:04.140
unique and just turned out difficult to handle.

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:05.940
Am I the only one?

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:07.080
Yeah, I got that a little bit.

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:08.820
Where the physics are a little odd.

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:12.260
I'm never quite sure how high my guy can jump also.

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:13.880
How high Hal can jump.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:17.860
Because sometimes it seems like if you stand in place and jump twice, I feel like the second

00:05:17.860 --> 00:05:18.740
jump goes higher.

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:23.040
Yeah, you have to time your jumps consecutively, but you have to time them, like, almost perfectly.

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:26.440
Like, sometimes I would miss the right timing and I would still jump the same height on the

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:27.700
second time and on the third time.

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:32.720
But then there are plenty of platforms in this game that I am not certain I can get to, if

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:34.860
I can get to or not, for, like, ten minutes.

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:36.920
And then I'm like, oh, yeah, I could have gotten to that.

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:39.100
I just had to hit it exactly perfectly.

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:42.100
Where, like, other things where I'm, like, still pretty certain I never could have gotten

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:43.780
to it, but, like, there's a little bit of doubt in my mind.

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:48.240
Like, maybe there's that perfect, like, frame-perfect input I can put in to get to

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:54.980
that platform. And that, to me, was, like, what made this different from all the other platformers we've

00:05:54.980 --> 00:05:56.580
played so far. Yeah.

00:05:56.920 --> 00:06:01.300
Like, I'd say I'd agree with Mike that it's sort of like an adventure game with a lot of

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:02.600
puzzle platform elements.

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:09.660
It does have a wonky physics engine, I guess, in that, like, there are three jump heights

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:17.640
and you have to land two jumps in rhythm to get to, like, that maximum third jump height,

00:06:17.680 --> 00:06:20.560
which is only slightly higher than the second.

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:30.720
There's also a weird way to go faster by, like, I guess just, like, spamming the attack

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:32.140
button while you're moving.

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:37.480
And all of this is to make the puzzles exist.

00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:46.580
Because, really, there aren't that many different things that are going on that make any one screen

00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:54.300
have a puzzle in it to, like, either get a key or get a very specific jump in, which is sort of why you

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:57.640
have to worry about how many jumps in a row you've made.

00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:01.800
Or to just guess at what blocks to blow up.

00:07:02.680 --> 00:07:04.680
Those are really the...

00:07:04.680 --> 00:07:09.740
That's the tool set for the puzzles in this, like, labyrinth game.

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:45.040
That's the tool set for the puzzles. Information on the screen is very strangely conveyed to you, though.

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:50.500
So, like, there are power-ups hidden that you might never even know about, to be honest.

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:53.700
Because a lot of them are just, like, hidden in the walls of things or something.

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:57.060
Not many of these power-ups are just, like, laying out there for you.

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:57.940
And who knows?

00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:03.260
Maybe that's neat. But, I don't know, like, once you collect them, they don't, like...

00:08:03.260 --> 00:08:06.700
There's no, like, pause menu where you can see your abilities and stuff like that.

00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:07.820
You just have them now.

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:12.640
And then there's, like, your location, which doesn't really matter.

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:16.660
It's, like, a, you know, like, a number dash letter thing.

00:08:16.820 --> 00:08:20.000
But you're never really, like, getting lost or in a particular...

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:21.780
It's not really, like, a maze.

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:24.780
You know, you are progressing from screen to screen.

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:29.920
So, that feels strange to give, like, information there where instead it could have been dedicated to, like, power-ups.

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:33.440
When you collect keys, you can only have, like, one at a time, I'm pretty sure.

00:08:33.680 --> 00:08:35.040
And it says key.

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:36.680
And they all open everything.

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:40.180
Yeah. And it's key in the top right or what have you.

00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:42.100
But even... Forget about, like, the UI.

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:49.700
Why? The game conveys the platforming elements really strange, too, where it's, like, this would have been a block.

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:51.260
And now, because it's a...

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:52.220
It lets you jump higher.

00:08:52.220 --> 00:08:55.940
They put, like, a spring on the, like...

00:08:55.940 --> 00:08:58.020
On the data of where the block would be.

00:08:58.120 --> 00:09:01.480
So, it doesn't feel like it's a spring that you jump onto.

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:05.840
It feels like this is a spring block that's, like, buried into the stage.

00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:07.760
I don't know if I'm making sense there.

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:09.620
Yeah. But, like, I just thought they were so strange.

00:09:09.620 --> 00:09:10.820
Right, Sam? Yeah.

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:17.960
It's the same with the skull blocks, which is just, like, a skull underneath a block that if you stand on it, it hurts you.

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:21.040
Right. And those hurt you, which I get.

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:22.040
Like, okay, that...

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:23.340
Sure, those are the ones that hurt you.

00:09:23.420 --> 00:09:24.660
That seems a little strange, right?

00:09:24.800 --> 00:09:26.660
But then there's spikes later on.

00:09:26.740 --> 00:09:31.300
So, why didn't they just go with spikes instead of having skull platforms?

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:38.600
That always felt to me, like, when I was a little kid trying to draw something in, like, a perspective that I didn't understand.

00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:40.420
You know? And I was, like...

00:09:40.420 --> 00:09:41.480
You know what I mean? No, I do.

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:42.800
Like, I'm trying to, like, draw, like...

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:50.960
Like, someone standing in the distance or somebody, like, standing, like, depth-wise into the page and they would just end up, like, up.

00:09:51.140 --> 00:09:53.440
Or, like, dying. Like, it wouldn't make any sense visually.

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:56.460
Like, that's how... But you didn't quite understand...

00:09:56.460 --> 00:10:01.240
You didn't quite understand, like, two-point perspective or whatever the hell that term is.

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:04.460
Yeah. Yeah, I kind of get that.

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:11.400
It is so weird that they would, like, choose to just, like, symbolize something when they could obviously just draw it.

00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:15.960
Like they had later in the game, like you guys are talking about.

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:17.200
I don't know.

00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:18.420
This is...

00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:20.920
This is square, isn't it?

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:24.100
I think they published the game.

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:25.260
I don't think they made it.

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:27.600
Oh, I thought they were the same thing.

00:10:28.220 --> 00:10:29.040
Yeah, no, no, no.

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:31.440
No. Oh, yeah. Of course.

00:10:33.020 --> 00:10:35.180
Yeah, I mean, you know, sometimes that's true.

00:10:35.340 --> 00:10:37.540
Nintendo publishes and develops a lot of stuff.

00:10:37.740 --> 00:10:43.560
But I went to go look up who made this game and it turns out there's a TV show called Mystery Quest.

00:10:43.720 --> 00:10:44.780
Does that piss off anybody?

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:49.460
Like, the TV show has nothing to do with the video game but also gets such a generic title?

00:10:50.220 --> 00:10:51.220
That sounds familiar.

00:10:51.560 --> 00:10:52.480
Is that a recent film?

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:53.860
Yes, recent.

00:10:54.580 --> 00:10:58.200
2010s. It looks like this was developed by Cary Lab.

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:03.320
Cary Lab, published by Square a little bit, maybe.

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:07.900
I see, yeah, dog is what they say, but then it links you to Square.

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:08.900
That's so strange.

00:11:09.620 --> 00:11:11.300
Naughty Dog was involved, I think.

00:11:11.680 --> 00:11:14.360
To answer your question, though, it does piss me off.

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:21.100
Okay, good. But wasn't Mystery Quest the TV show like a satire or like a, you know, it was like a funny show?

00:11:22.120 --> 00:11:25.900
I think you're talking about a very recent game.

00:11:26.420 --> 00:11:27.520
Wait, oh, never mind.

00:11:27.680 --> 00:11:29.720
That is a show that's currently running, right?

00:11:30.020 --> 00:11:31.460
No, that's Mystic Quest.

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:33.080
Mystic Quest, same thing.

00:11:33.560 --> 00:11:35.860
No, that's the Final Fantasy spinoff game.

00:11:35.980 --> 00:11:41.300
There was a Final Fantasy game called Mystic Quest on the Game Boy, and now that's got a TV show.

00:11:41.460 --> 00:11:43.200
Not based on Final Fantasy, of course.

00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:46.140
But let's get back to Mystery Quest for a second.

00:11:46.360 --> 00:11:48.700
I've got to talk about these enemies with you guys.

00:11:48.820 --> 00:11:49.960
What were they thinking?

00:11:50.080 --> 00:11:51.360
What is going on here?

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:55.200
You could play this whole game without even having to touch any of the enemies, right?

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:56.620
Like, they're small.

00:11:56.860 --> 00:11:58.020
You can jump over them.

00:11:58.020 --> 00:12:05.440
There's no need to defeat any of them other than like the, I don't know, what you call them, sub-bosses or bosses of the levels, the ones that give you the keys.

00:12:05.640 --> 00:12:07.460
Like, those guys maybe are a little more intimidating.

00:12:07.820 --> 00:12:12.620
But the fact that you're just fighting like guys that are smaller than you the whole game just feels very strange.

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:13.620
But they jump in your face.

00:12:13.720 --> 00:12:14.780
They like get in your way.

00:12:15.520 --> 00:12:17.400
Yeah, but just take a little bit of damage.

00:12:17.400 --> 00:12:20.980
You have a vitality bar that tells you how much health you have.

00:12:21.100 --> 00:12:22.400
But I need those.

00:12:22.740 --> 00:12:27.680
I need those for, because those sub-bosses, like, they can get pretty cheesy.

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:35.620
Like, the one, the first one that I came across was like a praying mantis sort of thing that just shot out like yellow glowing energy.

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:41.020
And that, like, the enemy can shoot through walls, but you sure can't.

00:12:41.120 --> 00:12:42.800
And it just like stays in the edges.

00:12:43.020 --> 00:12:43.900
It was just annoying.

00:12:44.100 --> 00:12:46.040
There was nothing challenging about it.

00:12:46.060 --> 00:12:48.620
It was just annoying. Similar to the enemies then.

00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:53.700
If they charge at you and stuff, then you can take care of them pretty easily or just jump over them.

00:12:53.760 --> 00:12:56.540
I feel like a pacifist run can be done of this game.

00:12:58.560 --> 00:13:01.040
Also, it's very generous with your vitality.

00:13:01.240 --> 00:13:03.380
Like, when you get hit, it does not take that much down.

00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:05.380
You replenish it a lot.

00:13:05.540 --> 00:13:11.140
Even though it is one of those games that is constantly draining vitality as time goes on, which I always hate.

00:13:11.400 --> 00:13:17.500
In this case, it drains it like the tiniest sliver every, like, 30 seconds or something.

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:19.760
Not if you get the super cape, Joe.

00:13:20.140 --> 00:13:21.660
Oh, well, I didn't even need it.

00:13:21.660 --> 00:13:29.280
If you get Superman's cape, which for some reason is in the game, it's actually like a red cape with an S on the back and everything.

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:33.720
That will prevent you from losing a little bit of health over time.

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:40.320
But again, that's not just something that's, like, out in the open or, you know, hidden in a dungeon or you got to get a key.

00:13:40.620 --> 00:13:42.940
These things are just, like, hidden in the game.

00:13:42.940 --> 00:13:46.100
And I just feel like that's just such a random design decision to have.

00:13:46.340 --> 00:13:48.720
Imagine if, like, Gradius only hid the power-ups.

00:13:48.880 --> 00:13:56.080
Like, you had to hit, like, blocks that you shouldn't be hitting in order to find the power-ups for your ship.

00:13:56.080 --> 00:13:57.860
It doesn't sit well with me.

00:13:58.040 --> 00:14:00.060
Well, it stands poor with me as well.

00:14:00.460 --> 00:14:29.140
There you go. We talked about that I don't like the enemies.

00:14:30.260 --> 00:14:34.460
We kind of have talked about these power-ups, but I feel like we could talk a little bit more about them, right?

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:37.320
Like, did anybody collect any of the power-ups?

00:14:40.260 --> 00:14:41.440
The role of magic?

00:14:41.800 --> 00:14:43.880
I had a couple, I think.

00:14:43.880 --> 00:14:52.640
I had the one that allows you to jump and, like, sort of break blocks with your head.

00:14:53.380 --> 00:14:54.560
The power-boots.

00:14:54.960 --> 00:14:56.860
I think that's the power-helmet.

00:14:58.800 --> 00:15:01.200
I think the boots make you stomp on them.

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:03.220
Oh, okay, gotcha.

00:15:03.320 --> 00:15:10.980
Yeah, yeah, yeah. So you're saying the helmet lets you break the blocks with your head, but the power-boots break them with your feet.

00:15:11.540 --> 00:15:13.360
Yeah, that's sort of what I'm saying.

00:15:13.820 --> 00:15:15.680
But it's only on specific sections, right?

00:15:15.760 --> 00:15:16.840
Like, you can't do it with every block.

00:15:16.840 --> 00:15:18.360
Only specific blocks, yeah.

00:15:18.880 --> 00:15:21.420
It's just the key. Are those told to you?

