Who wrote those famous lines?

00:25:42.340 --> 00:25:44.680
That's a quote from, who said that again?

00:25:47.020 --> 00:25:48.020
Nobuo Iwametsu.

00:25:49.820 --> 00:25:51.680
All right, wait, wait, real fast, real fast.

00:25:52.700 --> 00:25:56.180
Since we're talking about the endings and then the difference between the Japanese and the English,

00:25:56.380 --> 00:26:03.180
I think it's just worth noting that the Japanese version of this game, How's Mystery Adventure, what have you,

00:26:03.880 --> 00:26:07.360
that is, like, an actual full game.

00:26:07.560 --> 00:26:13.320
Like, for some reason when this came over, for no limitations of the cartridge or anything like that,

00:26:13.440 --> 00:26:14.500
they just started removing.

00:26:14.920 --> 00:26:17.560
Like, they removed three different castles.

00:26:17.820 --> 00:26:20.080
They removed, like, four power-ups.

00:26:20.320 --> 00:26:26.320
There's just, like, so much less of a game in Mystery Quest as opposed to How's Mystery Adventure.

00:26:26.320 --> 00:26:30.200
Sure, it's boggling to think that there are four extra castles.

00:26:30.400 --> 00:26:33.440
Did they just ship, like, an incomplete build or something?

00:26:33.600 --> 00:26:38.100
Is that, like, that would make more sense to me than, like, let's just take all this out.

00:26:38.180 --> 00:26:44.380
Yeah. It's a good question because I'm pretty sure How's Mystery Quest was on the Famicom Disk System,

00:26:44.640 --> 00:26:50.080
but technically, like, other than, like, some extra sound and stuff like that, I'm pretty sure.

00:26:50.200 --> 00:26:51.160
Look, I'm not an expert.

00:26:51.160 --> 00:26:56.880
I'm just saying I'm pretty sure that a lot of Famicom Disk System games translated over to the NES just fine

00:26:56.880 --> 00:26:59.700
and just messed, you know, just a different sound system.

00:26:59.700 --> 00:27:05.540
So I'm not sure why, you know, like, they would be like, no, we don't, like, we don't have room for this.

00:27:05.660 --> 00:27:07.440
We got to remove four dungeons.

00:27:07.700 --> 00:27:09.920
Like, don't even include the game then.

00:27:10.100 --> 00:27:12.660
Like, it went from three levels to six.

00:27:12.840 --> 00:27:13.840
Like, it's crazy.

00:27:14.840 --> 00:27:15.720
Crazy Taxi.

00:27:15.880 --> 00:27:17.020
Crazy Taxi is right.

00:27:17.540 --> 00:27:18.380
Crazy Frog.

00:27:19.160 --> 00:27:20.820
Yeah, Crazy Frog as well.

00:27:21.040 --> 00:27:22.000
Lots of crazy things.

00:27:22.240 --> 00:27:27.100
Oh, yeah. I don't have anything in the sequels and spinoff section here,

